      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm helping organize a medical symposium in Geneva next month. Can you help me draft a minute-by-minute logistics timeline for the opening ceremony on Day 1? I need to account for speaker arrivals, AV/tech setup, catering arrival, and the actual start of the keynote. It's a pretty tight schedule so I need it to be very precise.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Day 1, October 15th - Medical Symposium Opening Ceremony\n\n08:00 AM - Attendees, speakers, and VIPs arrive at the Geneva Convention Center lobby.\n\n08:30 AM - Catering arrives and sets up refreshments in the foyer.\n\n08:45 AM - Attendees check-in at the registration desk and are greeted with name tags and brochures.\n\n09:00 AM - Security personnel ensures all guests have checked in and conducts security check.\n\n09:10 AM - Technical team begins AV and tech setup in the main conference hall.\n\n09:30 AM - AV team heads to the delegates' lounge to connect cables and projectors.\n\n09:45 AM - Final technical rehearsal before the keynote.\n\n10:00 AM - Doors open for attendees to enter the main conference hall and find seats according to a prearranged seating plan.\n\n10:10 AM - Markers placed at the podium for speaker ease of movement.\n\n10:15 AM - Attendees are ushered to their seats by designated liaisons.\n\n10:30 AM - Keynote speaker arrives on the stage holding the microphone cord.\n\n10:31 AM - Speaker begins introduction, followed by a brief Q&A session.\n\n10:45 AM - Breakout Social Hour with light snacks,",
